and to modify and share under the same license; inclusion in commercial or closed-source
miners needs written permission from suprnova.cc. Versions up to v0.5.4 stay under their
MIT-with-restriction license. The miner contains no
third-party source code: the Ed25519 field arithmetic, the ECVRF construction (RFC 9381,
ECVRF-EDWARDS25519-SHA512-TAI) and SHA-512 are implemented in this repository. Test vectors
in vectors.json were generated with the Proxima node's own util/vrf package
(https://github.com/lunfardo314/proxima, Apache-2.0); no Proxima code is distributed here.

Binaries link the NVIDIA CUDA runtime statically under the CUDA Toolkit EULA
(https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/eula/); the NVIDIA driver on the host is required.

Windows release archives also include, unmodified, for stratum+ssl:// connections:
- OpenSSL 3 (libssl-3-x64.dll, libcrypto-3-x64.dll), Apache License 2.0, https://www.openssl.org/
  (licence text in LICENSE-OpenSSL.txt when the build provides it).
- cacert.pem, the Mozilla CA certificate bundle as published by the curl project
  (https://curl.se/docs/caextract.html), Mozilla Public License 2.0.
On Linux the miner uses the system's OpenSSL and CA store; nothing is bundled.
